# Copy to .env (ignored by git and by the image build) and fill in what you have.
# Every line is optional. With none of them set, PACT runs end to end on the
# simulated rail, with the deterministic gate and no Claude agent.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   PACT_PROFILE=paypal-agentic docker compose up --build    # http://localhost:8080

# --- which event -------------------------------------------------------------
# razorpay-track01 (rupees, the default) | upi-agentic (rupees) | paypal-agentic (dollars)
PACT_PROFILE=

# --- PayPal (sandbox only; the client refuses any other host) ----------------
# From a sandbox app at developer.paypal.com, with vaulting enabled in its
# settings. With both set, the paypal-agentic profile settles on PayPal.
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The id PayPal gives the webhook you register against your deployed URL.
# Without it every PayPal webhook is refused; the reconciler still settles.
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
# A vaulted sandbox wallet for mandates that never connected one of their own.
# scripts/paypal_sandbox.py prints one after you approve as a sandbox buyer.
PAYPAL_VAULT_ID=

# --- Claude -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Turns on the Claude buyer (/api/agent) and the gate's intent auditor (check
# ten). Without it the agent refuses runs with a 503 and the gate runs its nine
# deterministic checks plus the pattern scan.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides. Defaults: claude-opus-5-5; agent effort medium, auditor
# effort low; the auditor's budget is 800 ms. Measure before changing them:
# scripts/measure_auditor.py.
# PACT_AGENT_MODEL=
# PACT_AGENT_EFFORT=
# AUDITOR_MODEL=
# AUDITOR_EFFORT=
# AUDITOR_TIMEOUT_MS=

# --- the agent service's limits on a hosted demo ------------------------------
# PACT_AGENT_RUNS_PER_HOUR=
# PACT_AGENT_RUNS_AT_ONCE=

# --- Razorpay (test keys only: the client refuses anything not rzp_test_) ---
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
